WEBVTT

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.210
Who the heck are you?
A new type of Red Bug?

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.170
Huh? You are...?

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.720
I'm a human...at least I think so...

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.930
Anyways, I'm not a Red Bug.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.310
But who are you? Could you tell me...

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:25.230
Shut up. Island Six
sure is full of strange stuff.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:31.360
Take that.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.250
A bug with good eyes. Not bad.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.670
Then how about this?

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.050
Ouch...

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.470
That hurt.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:05.770
Hey, that's Midori-chan!

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.400
Where'd you get it? You can use it?

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:12.110
Ritsu-san gave it to me.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:16.280
Yeah? You know Ritsu?

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:23.790
Inside the dark my heartbeat echoes

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.670
Long night will continue on

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:34.260
Time to face the hell that surrounds you
Before you crash and burn

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:37.630
Within the fire
Your soul will rise now

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:57.070
Breathe in, breathe out
Your blank gaze on the brink of life

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:03.870
Step hard on the accelerator now
Escape the tunnel and overtake that pain

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:10.880
A shadow disappears into smoke

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:18.720
Lost light will continue on tomorrow

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:25.850
Someday our world will change
Inside a fantasy Remember, remember

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:32.940
I will mercilessly break your dream
and steal it away, with these hands

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:39.320
Until this body breaks
Beyond the limit We'll never surrender

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:42.740
Endless agony

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.000
Finding my life in the KEMURIKUSA

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.420
Oh, so you're with Ritsu huh?

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.380
Then bug or not, I'm cool.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.710
Okay, but I'm not a bug.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:04.100
Anyways, have a seat.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:05.970
Okay...

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.350
So this hairy thing is with Ritsu, huh?

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.610
Glad to see they're having fun.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:17.360
Hey, are you what they call animals?

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:20.740
I guess I'm sort of an animal.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.780
But I'm more human, I think.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:26.870
You don't speak too clearly.
What's your name?

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.620
W-Wakaba!

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.620
I'm Riku.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.330
Nice to meet you.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.880
Hey, you have a sense of touch?

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.180
Like this? Yes, to a normal extent.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:54.190
-How's this?
-Uh, yes.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.570
-And this?
-Ouch, that hurts.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.360
What about this? Huh?

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:03.320
Ticklish...and kind of embarrassing.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:08.160
Wow, finally somebody I can talk to!

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.540
It tingles when someone
strokes your back, right?

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:18.170
Yes, I guess it does.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:21.470
Nobody really gets it.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.300
And pain is something else.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:26.800
Makes you feel so alive.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:30.140
Uh, not really. You scare me.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.680
Scratch my back, will ya?

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.900
Huh? Uh, okay.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.770
Yes, that's the spot.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.950
This is so great.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.950
It's just not the same
if you do it yourself.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:50.660
Ritsu was really good at it.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.000
You know her?

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:56.210
Duh, we were born together.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:00.210
You mean, you're one of the sisters?

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:03.340
Right on. How are they all doing?

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:05.760
They're doing great.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:10.640
Ritsu-san too. And Rina-san hops around
looking for something to eat.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:13.930
Hasn't changed a bit, huh?

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:17.730
How's Rin? Still crying like a baby?

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.860
She'd cry whenever something happened.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.570
No, never. She's always very undaunted.

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.910
Huh? Undaunted?

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:31.870
Putting on a front like that.

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:37.920
She should hurry up and
find something she likes and just be lazy.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:41.750
She's so serious, it's crazy.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:45.220
So, where are you guys going?

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:46.880
Still got water?

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:51.010
Yes, but only a little bit.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:56.270
So we're looking for the lake.
We're going to a new place tomorrow.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:59.940
I see. That's why you're here.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:03.690
Yeah, the water is pretty close.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.570
What are you doing here?

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:12.120
Me? Well, I guess you could say
I'm doing preliminary investigation.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:15.120
Figuring out what it's all about.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.330
"It"?

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:21.250
You feel it over there?

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.130
Kind of warm, right?

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.470
Sorry, but I don't feel it.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:34.970
You still have a ways to go.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:39.640
Anyways, you all stay away.
We'll deal with it.

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:44.900
You just used Kemurikusa, didn't you?

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:47.110
You're really good at it.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:50.450
Could you teach me how to use it?

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.490
Huh?

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:55.410
I got stuff to do.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:57.790
Please, Riku-san.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:02.210
Don't ask me. Just touch it
and figure it out for yourself.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:07.090
If I could use it like you,
I could be of use to everyone.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.720
Please!

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:15.010
Well, you scratched my back,
so just a tad.

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.270
Show me your leaves.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:19.060
Yes!

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:21.730
All you're doing is pushing.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:30.450
Push, then push harder, right?
And it throbs, right?

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:34.910
Circles come up, so you choose one.
And it glows, got it?

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:38.830
-Like this?
-Nah, like this.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.870
Gosh, you're so clumsy.

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:43.880
Oh, I see!

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.800
This leaf feels like a wall.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.760
I did it!

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:52.510
Way different from just pushing, eh?

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:54.390
Wow, amazing.

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:57.430
You can control the power and effect.

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:02.890
Some are pretty complicated.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.940
Get used to it, and you can use double.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:15.620
Okay, now get ready.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.620
Gotta be able to use it in combat.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:25.420
I'll shoot once. Learn the quick way.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:32.220
No, you really don't have to!
I'll practice and get used to it!

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:35.640
Guys like you freeze up in combat.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:37.050
Brace yourself.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:39.720
Will I be okay even if it hits me?

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:43.020
What good would it be if it were?

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:45.480
Get ready or you'll die.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:48.520
Ready?

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.160
Um, push harder and...

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:58.870
After it throbs, choose, and...

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:13.260
Far from perfect, but you get the idea.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.190
Thank you.

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:30.060
Later. I still gotta investigate
a bit more.

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:33.940
Aren't you going to go see your sisters?

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:36.070
They'll be glad to see you.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.410
I'm supposed to be gone.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:42.370
They're better off on their own.

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:51.840
Before you go, could you tell me
more about this place, or this world?

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:54.630
Did there used to be lots of people?

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:59.470
Don't ask me. I don't care about
what happened before I was born.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:01.220
I'm not Ryoku.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:05.730
What's fun is thinking about
feeling new things.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:11.270
For me, it's more like
what to do for the end.

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:13.940
Hey, why don't you ask Ryoku?

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:15.690
Hey!

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:18.570
Asleep, huh.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:25.450
Hey, you got that rough one
that Ritsu had?

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.750
You mean, this?

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:34.210
It'll tell you what you want to know.
Use it like the other one.

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:35.210
Later.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.300
Thank you. For everything.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:41.890
Go straight and you'll get to Ritsu.

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:44.760
I forgot, I was lost.

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:49.060
And take this. You're almost out, right?

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.780
Is this Ai-san?

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:02.160
What a strange person.

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:04.660
Oh yeah.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:08.410
Don't tell my sisters about me.

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:11.500
We're supposed to be gone, ya know.

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:14.500
Okay...

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:18.760
You work extra hard for me. Later.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.050
That strangeness.

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:24.430
They're sisters without a doubt.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:29.980
Like this, and this.

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:34.360
I'm totally getting the hang of it. Great!

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:39.440
I can change the effect and power
by how I touch these circles.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:43.070
I could probably use the others too.

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:45.990
Oh yeah, I'm going to try Daidai-san.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.710
Wow, she was right. I can read it.

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:59.380
I see. I can open it
by touching them longer.

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:01.630
I can see multiple ones at once.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.760
It moved! Oh wow.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:11.020
"On how this world works..."

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:13.770
ON HOW THIS WORLD WORKS...

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:17.940
LOOKS LIKE I CAN WRITE THIS MYSELF,
SO HERE I GO.

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:21.610
SO MUCH I WANT TO KNOW,
BUT FIRST WE MUST SURVIVE.

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:25.450
KEMURIKUSA SEEM TO BE VITAL.
SHAME ONLY RIKU CAN USE THEM.

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:31.700
IT SEEMS WE AND KEMURIKUSA
NEED WATER AS ENERGY.

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:35.380
THIS WORLD IS MADE OF ISLANDS.
WALLS IN BETWEEN?

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:38.420
LOTS OF PEOPLE WERE HERE BEFORE?
WHERE'D THEY GO?

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:43.930
LETTERS ARE USEFUL. DECIPHERING THESE
HARD ONES WOULD LEAD TO MORE INFO.

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:48.680
THE FIRST PERSON IS HIDING SOMETHING?
CAN WE TRUST THEM?

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:53.140
Wow, this is incredible.
I can understand it.

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:57.480
The person who wrote this is amazing.
Just what I wanted to know.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:01.730
I guess they were researching this world.
Wow.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:06.360
Come to think of it, walls are
a strange way to connect islands.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:10.280
Maybe it has to do with the earthquakes?

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:15.040
The person who wrote this
isn't a bad person.

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:18.670
They're worried about Rin and the others.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:23.590
Definitely sounds like a sister.

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:27.970
I wonder if it says more about Kemurikusa.

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:30.470
Does it have any pages on it?

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:36.850
I want to read more. What to read next...

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:39.270
Huh?

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:40.610
AFTER I AM SPLIT UP.

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:45.190
The writing is different from here.

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:46.610
Let me see.

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:51.910
TO MYSELF AFTER SPLITTING. IF YOU'RE
READING THIS, SOME TROUBLE CAME UP?

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:57.250
ONE OF ME SHOULD HAVE THE MEMORY LEAF.
ASKING HER SHOULD ANSWER MOST QUESTIONS.

00:13:57.420 --> 00:14:02.050
THOUGH UNLIKELY, IF THE MEMORY LEAF
DOESN'T WORK, OPEN IT A FEW TIMES.

00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:06.170
AFTER SPLITTING, YOU'LL MOVE WITH
KEMURIKUSA. KEEP DRINKING WATER.

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:11.470
YOU CAN READ, RIGHT? YOU'VE READ ALL THIS?
SHARE THIS WITH THOSE WHO CAN'T READ.

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:15.310
LASTLY, JUST IN CASE, OUR MISSION IS...

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:21.150
SORRY, YOU CAN FORGET THIS. LIVE FREELY
AS YOU WISH. THE MEMORY LEAF TOO...

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:24.650
A mistake?

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:27.530
I wonder who wrote what?

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:31.570
Either Ryoku-san or Ryo-san?

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:33.740
Hey!

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:44.340
Where did you wander off to?

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:46.420
We thought you were gone.

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:47.800
We're going.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:49.720
Sorry.

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:56.100
You didn't sleep much?

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:57.890
What were you doing?

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:00.810
I got lost picking Kemurikusa.

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:02.690
Oh, and...

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:06.530
Just over there, I...

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:10.070
I mean, no, nothing.

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:12.490
What?

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.450
You're suspicious.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:18.160
Are you hogging something yummy?

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:21.670
No, not at all! I just walked around.

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:24.250
You didn't have to come back.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:25.750
That's mean!

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:27.920
Anyways, let's go.

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:30.300
-Okay!
-Okay...

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:33.470
You didn't get to sleep much, did you?

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:36.310
Why don't you sleep while we move?

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.230
No, I'm fine. I'll stay on watch.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:46.230
Island Six really is a labyrinth.

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:48.150
We have to be careful.

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:53.450
We don't have a map beyond Island Six.

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:57.410
It's a dead-end to the left.

00:15:57.580 --> 00:16:00.620
If you want to go deeper,
you'll want to go right.

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:02.710
What a great help!

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:04.380
Nice going, Wakaba.

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:18.310
Ai-chan says to go this way.

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:20.350
We'll have to go around it.

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:23.020
Look, Ai-chan...

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:30.490
I guess it's really over.

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:33.490
We'd been using it for a long time.

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:35.030
Thank you, Ai-chan.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:36.240
You did well.

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:39.540
We're in a pinch now.

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:41.410
What should we do?

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:44.170
It was pointing that way just now.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:52.340
But it's too dark to see.
We'll have to be careful.

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:55.680
I'll try to remember the roads we take.

00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:59.220
Thanks. I'll add to the map too.

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:04.440
We don't have much water,
so we shouldn't all walk.

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:14.110
Do you think you could use this?

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:25.040
Is this Ai-chan?

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:26.710
-Yes!
-It is!

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:29.040
Where did you get this?

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:32.800
I got this from...uh, I found it.

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:37.970
That's incredible, Wakaba-kun.
You just made it glow.

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:39.470
Good one, Wakaba.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:41.720
You're kind of like Sis Riku.

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:46.890
This really is Ai. We'll use it.

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:50.110
Please do. I'm glad to be of help.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:53.150
We won't get too off course now.

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:15.880
Considering the size of the island,
we should be nearing the wall.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:20.470
We're in trouble if red fog comes.
We need to go somewhere open.

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:22.810
We're almost out of water too.

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:27.390
Does Island Seven really even exist?

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:30.020
What if this continues forever?

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:33.150
I don't want to think about that.

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:36.280
Hey, is this...

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:40.620
From this way.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.750
It's the same tree as Midori-chan.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:58.340
Really, the same?
But the color is different.

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:00.430
The sound is the same.

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:03.100
Actually, I've seen this before.

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:07.180
You mean, you can move this too?

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:09.440
I don't know.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:23.780
It's no good. Doesn't budge an inch.

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:25.410
It's huge too.

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:28.750
Most of the branches are dead.

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:30.960
This...

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:33.750
It's probably wilted.

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:38.170
The sound doesn't go far,
and it's broken here and there.

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:44.890
I wonder if it says anything
about Midori-san.

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:47.180
Like this, and...

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:52.560
Let me see, where is it?

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:54.520
That's...!

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:56.940
I found it!

00:19:57.110 --> 00:20:01.360
Here. "About green Kemurikusa."

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:07.330
"Green Kemurikusa will be
a great help to us."

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:11.540
"But there aren't any old ones
around here either."

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:15.170
"They'll probably be close to a lake."

00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:17.880
Yes, you're right.

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:21.170
We didn't even think about that at first.

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:25.140
You can read that? When did you learn to?

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:30.560
Yes, Ri...
I mean, I kind of figured it out.

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:34.980
Let me see what else it says.

00:20:37.360 --> 00:20:41.150
"If you find a large, living Kemurikusa
with branches."

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:44.660
"Even if it's withered,
if it has long branches and roots,

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:47.830
there may be lots of water nearby."

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:55.500
"There should be some kind of
Kemurikusa tree by the lake."

00:20:55.670 --> 00:21:00.300
"Follow it and you might find
a lake or at least some water."

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:04.840
"However, it may not
be a safe Kemurikusa."

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:09.140
"So I can't tell my sisters yet."

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:13.020
"My stupid sisters will try too hard.
I can't let them do that."

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:16.060
"I couldn't bear to watch."

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:17.690
Ryoku-chan...

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:26.280
It's pointing the same way.

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:29.490
Let's walk along these roots.

00:21:59.610 --> 00:22:00.650
What...?
